question battling over the economy the  pandemic and president rodrigo duterte's  policies they debate in front of a live  audience who has the best plan for the  country's future  manila mayor isco moreno senator panfilo  luxon and vice president leni robredo  are among the crowd favorites  out of 118. out of the 118  infrastructure plans of president  duterte only 12 have been finished we  need to rebuke them and instead get the  filipino private sector as partners also  focusing less on infrastructure and  going beyond like linking farms to  market roads  known around the world for his boxing  career manny pacquiao is now a senator  promising to provide housing for all  filipino families but he hasn't exactly  laid out how he plans to achieve that  just like manny pacquiao manila mayor  istory  is quintessentially filipino he was a  poor kid who became an actor he went on  to become one of manila's most popular  mayors  moreno doubled down on that rags to  riches story saying anything is possible  if he becomes president  vice president leni robredo is the  leader of the opposition and the only  female candidate in this year's run-up  let us not look for the ones who are not  here i am always here all the time in  front of you  fighting for you  true leaders show up and man up  the best man for the job is a woman mr  marcos will not be joining this debate  robredo is referring to this empty  podium it was meant for bongbong marcus  jr son of the late dictator ferdinand  marcus senior and a front-runner in the  elections but he has refused to attend  nearly all debates since the campaign  started he says the questions have been  repetitive and are lacking in substance  some of those questions include his  conviction for tax evasion his family's  multi-million dollar estate tax and  accusations over drugs use  even his own supporters have urged him  to show up saying leaders should have  the courage to face the public compared  to previous debates the insults hurled  towards each other are less personal  but as the hours dragged on the show  started to look more like an emergency  meeting for a country deeply in crisis  in this key moment of a long and  divisive campaign nearly all the  candidates agree that debates are a  necessary opportunity for the voters to  measure the candidates credibility  jamella allendogen al jazeera manila
 

